## Common Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Using `any` type → ✅ Define explicit TypeScript interfaces
- ❌ Class components → ✅ Use functional components with hooks
- ❌ Prop drilling beyond 2 levels → ✅ Use context or state management
- ❌ Direct fetch in components → ✅ Abstract API calls into services
- ❌ Deploying frontend source → ✅ Build and deploy only static assets
- ❌ No error boundaries → ✅ Implement error boundaries for graceful failures
- ❌ Mixing concerns in components → ✅ Separate business logic into hooks/services

